course: dictionary
lesson: 2816
title: A rare, old-fashioned word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are rare, and you mostly meet them in old books. Distressful is one of them. It means causing pain, worry or sadness, or being full of trouble and suffering. Today people usually say «distressing» instead.
explain: Look at the words around it to find its meaning. «Never noticing his companion's silence and distressful state of mind.» The companion is silent, and his state of mind is distressful, so he must be unhappy and troubled. The clues point the same way as the meaning.
explain: Check by swapping in a meaning. Does «his unhappy and troubled state of mind» still make sense in the sentence? If it does, you have probably understood it. If it doesn't, read the sentence again, or look the word up in a dictionary.
fact: Distressful means causing pain, worry or sadness, or full of trouble and suffering.
fact: Distressful is a rare, slightly old-fashioned adjective. Today people usually say «distressing».
fact: «Distressful state of mind» means a troubled, unhappy way of thinking and feeling.
fact: An adjective describes a noun, such as a sight, a time, a journey or a state of mind.
exercise: «...never noticing his companion's silence and distressful state of mind.» What does distressful mean here? | Very fast and busy | Calm and relaxed | *Troubled and unhappy | Full of laughter
exercise: Which word is the everyday word people usually use today instead of distressful? | Dreary | *Distressing, which means upsetting | Distressing | Relaxing
exercise: An old book describes «distressful times». What does this suggest? | Sunny weather | Happy holidays by the sea | Quiet, peaceful days | *Hard times full of trouble
test: «The distressful cry came from the cold, dark wood.» What kind of cry was it? | *Upsetting and full of pain | Happy and loud | Quiet and sleepy | Funny and silly
test: Which word is closest in meaning to distressful? | Sleepy | *Upsetting | Tiny | Cheerful
exam: Lily reads «a distressful journey» and asks what it means. What is the best answer? | *A journey that was painful and full of trouble | A journey on a boat | A journey that was fast and easy | A journey full of laughter
